# Design Patterns

## Always
- Check if pattern exists in codebase
- Name the pattern when applying
- Explain why it fits the problem
- Keep it simple - pattern isn't always needed

## Avoid
- Pattern for pattern's sake
- Forcing patterns onto simple code
- Using Singleton (use DI instead)
- Abstract Factory when Factory suffices

## Common Patterns

| Problem | Pattern |
|---------|---------|
| Object with many optional fields | Builder |
| Create objects without exposing concrete class | Factory |
| Multiple algorithms, swap at runtime | Strategy |
| Object behavior changes with state | State |
| Notify multiple objects of changes | Observer |
| Undo/redo, command queue | Command |

## Pattern Smells
- Factory returning same type always
- Strategy with single implementation
- Observer with single listener

